# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# The page says where it is.  A program longer than the window wears a
# scrollbar in a gutter of its own -- the same bar the folders and the
# panels wear -- whose thumb stands where the view stands and whose
# track PAGES the view when pressed.  And the strip beneath says where
# the caret is: the line and column, and the NUMBER a BASIC line wears,
# which is the name the interpreter will call it by.
wait 25
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Programming
wait 4
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 150
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
click 400 220
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
click-window Project
wait 8
key Down
wait 8
key Return
wait 90
expect-title main.bas
note the strip says the caret's line and column, and the BASIC number
note -- text that the bare name and count never reached
expect-pixel 343 667 000000
note the page opened at its end, so the thumb stands at the BOTTOM of
note the track, with empty track above it
expect-pixel 803 350 b1b1b1
expect-pixel 803 500 d8d8d8
note a press high on the track pages the view UP, and the thumb comes
note with it: what was empty track is now the thumb, and the reverse
click 806 330
wait 20
expect-pixel 803 350 d8d8d8
expect-pixel 803 500 b1b1b1
quit
